{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"agent_message","text":"Yes, they still could be there, but I would treat it as **possible and probably rare**, not likely/common.\n\nWhat I found:\n- EBTL is in the **Krishnagiri-Melagiri foothill landscape** in Tamil Nadu, not an isolated site. Public EBTL pages place it near Budhimutlu in the eastern edge of the **Bilgiri-Melagiri hill complex**. Source: [EBTL site](https://ebtl.earth/), [research page](https://ebtl.earth/cegs/).\n- A 2018 public herpetofauna survey of the **Bilgiri-Melagiri massif and other Southern Eastern Ghats sites** recorded 37 snake species, but I did **not** find king cobra listed in that survey. Source: [Ganesh et al. 2018](https://www.researchgate.net/publication/331523059_Herpetofauna_of_Southern_Eastern_Ghats_India-II_From_Western_Ghats_to_Coromandel_Coast).\n- Public citizen-science checklists I found for **Krishnagiri** and **Melagiris** also did **not** show king cobra records. Sources: [Krishnagiri checklist](https://www.inaturalist.org/check_lists/316682-Krishnagiri-Check-List), [Melagiris checklist](https://www.inaturalist.org/check_lists/4104133-Melagiris-Check-List).\n- But king cobra is publicly recorded from **Tamil Nadu** and from the **Eastern Ghats more broadly**. Sources: [India Biodiversity Portal](https://indiabiodiversity.org/species/show/238894), [Eastern Ghats Wildlife Society](https://eghats.org/home/program/king-cobra-conservation), [Indian Reptiles](https://www.indianreptiles.org/ophiophagus-hannah).\n\nMy estimate:\n- **Inside EBTL itself:** possible, but I would guess **low probability at present**.\n- **In the wider nearby hill forest landscape:** more plausible, especially in **better forested, wetter, less disturbed patches** than the EBTL valley floor.\n- So the most careful wording is: **“No confirmed public record inside EBTL, but occasional presence in the surrounding landscape is still biologically plausible.”**\n\nWhat is missing:\n- No verified public record I found from **inside EBTL**.\n- No clear georeferenced public king cobra record from the **immediate Krishnagiri/Melagiri-EBTL vicinity**.\n- No local systematic snake survey, rescue log, or repeated night transects focused on king cobra habitat around EBTL.\n\nIf useful, I can next turn this into a **2-3 sentence NGO-ready note** or a **simple confidence table**."}}
